  "description": "<p>When we create placeholder resources, and then later update them with PUT, we should include the If-Unmodified-Since header to prevent accidentally overwriting any other changes that might happen in the meantime.</p>\n\n<p>Note, as discussed in \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-2478\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-2478\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Use POST with a Slug header instead of PUT\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10300?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-2478\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n, the LDP spec recommends using the If-Match header.  However, the non-fixed nature of RDF makes it impractical to use strong ETags (which are required by If-Match), so If-Unmodified-Since is the alternative.</p>",
